codex
**One serious finding remains:** the plan does not say how it will identify the same question across replay arms after question numbers change. For example, if the new arm merges away `v3`, a later, unrelated question can receive the number `v3`; comparing that number alone can make a wrong destination look right.

1. **Serious — the per-candidate check needs stable question identities across arms.** [Plan lines 114–117](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:114) record the expected destination as an existing question `X`, and [lines 153–164](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:153) compare that destination with each arm. But question IDs are assigned sequentially as questions are created ([writing.py, lines 22–25 and 37–38](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:22)). Removing one duplicate therefore shifts later IDs. The old replay script attempts translation by source item and question, but falls back to the old ID when it finds no match ([pinned_matching_study.py, lines 27–32 and 67–71](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-26-thesis-admission-v12/pinned_matching_study.py:27)). The plan requires that script to reproduce the control, but does not specify how to resolve an old question that the new arm has merged away. A control can reproduce perfectly while the changed arm compares or files evidence against the wrong `v3`. The check needs a traceable mapping from each gold question to its actual question in each arm, including merged-away questions, and must stop if that mapping cannot be established.

2. **Factual — the revenue/growth example misstates Jev’s verdict.** [Plan line 82](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:82) says Jev called v38’s total revenue and revenue growth questions unrelated. The [stored v38 ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28/views.sqlite), inspected through [why_new.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/why_new.py:13), records candidate `c3` against `v4` as `same_matter_different_quantity`, probability `0.69`. The different measure still prevents the collision comparison ([jev_matching.py, lines 195–201](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:195)); the recorded Jev reason should be corrected.

The round-4 structural rule now explicitly covers required successors, distinct but unworthy questions, and successor evidence; the future-deadline transition has a separate test ([plan lines 114–124 and 159–168](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:114)). The round-8 duplicate regression is also a per-candidate stop condition. Those checks can detect false merges and lost required questions **once the cross-arm identity problem above is resolved**.

I verified the main census counts by rerunning its read-only script on all five ledgers, and verified the 20 shared evidence records between v38 `v1` and `v3`. The census verdict categories remain provisional because the script parses reason text ([admission_census.py, lines 18–37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission_census.py:18)). I also checked the ACP archive: call 66 and call 236 compare different candidates, as the revised plan says. The guarantee-and-financing sentence is in both the [signed standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:316) and the [collision prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v1.txt:1); the stored reasons do not establish that it caused the split.

I found no additional uncovered hard case in the two ledgers that requires a new H1–H7 mechanism. The leans name the relevant standard boundaries, and H7 preserves D204. I could not independently verify every archived quotation, cost estimate, or the full question context behind Alex’s two recorded “A” replies; those remain unverified rather than assumed correct.

**Serious finding remains: yes — cross-arm question identity is not yet defined for the acceptance comparison.**
